  "description": "USat is a unified self-supervised encoder for multi-sensor satellite imagery, based on a vision transformer with modified patch projection layers and positional encodings to handle spectral bands with varying spatial scales from multiple sensors. It is pre-trained using a masked autoencoder (MAE) approach and supports flexible input of arbitrary subsets of spectral bands from multiple sensors.",
